<section class="content-section product-detail-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">BUYER'S GUIDE</p><h2>Make box-finding workflows easier to define</h2><p>A box-finding tool is only useful when it reflects the way a team identifies, stores and retrieves boxes. Start by documenting how boxes are labelled, what information is recorded, where items move and how staff search when something cannot be found.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Map the storage environment</h3><p>Describe shelves, zones, racks or storage locations and how staff currently identify a box.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Define the information needed</h3><p>Decide which identifiers, labels, status fields or search details staff need. Confirm which of these SHYFT currently supports.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Plan the day-to-day workflow</h3><p>Test common scenarios, including moved boxes, incomplete labels, duplicate identifiers and the process for updating records.</p></article></div></div></section>
